  "sourceTitle": "Pickled Quinces",
  "sourceText": "Pickled Quinces\nBy: Anonymous\nPublished: Saturday, February 13, 2010 - 2:51am\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\nSugar\nVinegar\nCayenne pepper\nCloves\nPeppercorns\nQuinces\n\nPreparation\n\n1 One pound of sugar to every pint of vinegar. 2 Cut the quinces in very small pieces, put in a preserving pan and nearly cover with vinegar. 3 Add spices and boil until tender. 4 Let cool and the pickle is ready for use.",
